[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n2_osric"
text = "# DRAFT
# Osric at the kitchen fire at dusk (night 2). Jolly; he carried the drowned merchant (he handles the bodies).
# He noticed whether the porter ate his bread last night (n1_ate_bread). Asking what's in the bread, once warned,
# is the wrong question to the wrong brother (Suspicion +5), and ends the talk on his question.
== start
(Osric at the kitchen fire again, red-faced from it. He waves a ladle at you.)
-> dead [if died_merchant]
-> ate [if n1_ate_bread]
-> left

== dead
Osric: A sad morning's work. I helped carry that merchant out of the pond, heavy as wet barley. Not kitchen talk.
-> ate [if n1_ate_bread]
-> left

== ate
Osric: You cleared your trencher last night! That's a porter I like.
-> topics

== left
Osric: You left your bread last night, brother. My bread! (He laughs, but his eyes stay on you.)
Osric: Tonight you'll eat it, or I'll know why.
-> topics

== again
Osric: Back for a taste? Not till the bell.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n2_osric_supper] What's for supper, brother? -> supper
* [if bread_warned] [if not n2_osric_bread] What's in the bread, brother? -> bread

== supper [set n2_osric_supper]
Osric: Eels, stewed, if the eelman got through the rain. He did. And the bread, with a heel put by for you.
-> topics

== bread [set n2_osric_bread] [suspicion 5]
Osric: In my bread? Rye and salt and water and my own two hands. Rye from our own granary.
(He keeps smiling. He has stopped kneading.)
Osric: Who's been talking to you about my bread, brother?
-> end

== leave
Osric: Come hungry, mind!
"
